From 182642aa863dd50d097c9e81932fd7ce2b2470df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hans de Goede <johannes.goede@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 14:59:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 204/263] drm: simplefb-resources: Add new simplefb resource
 helpers

The simpledrm (drm/kms) and simplefb (fbdev) drivers have a bunch of
duplicate code for managing clock / regulator / PM-domains described
in simple-framebuffer compatible DT-nodes.

Add a set of helpers implementing this functionality.

There are some differences between the mostly identical clk/regulator/pd
handling in simpledrm / simplefb and these new helpers.

1. clks/regulators/pd pointer array memory management:
- simpledrm uses devm() memory-management for this
- simplefb mixes devm() and manual memory-management for this

2. Disabling/release clks/regulators/pds on driver-detach vs fb_destroy()
- simpledrm uses devm_add_action() to disable/release on driver-detach
- simpleb manually disables/releasees from its fb_destroy() call-back

To avoid any behavior change here the new simplefb resource management
helpers manually alloc memory and rely on its user manually calling
simplefb_release_resources() to disable/release clk/regulator/pds and
free memory.

This way simplefb can simply call this from fb_destroy() and simepldrm
can register a single devm-action calling this, leaving the behavior
the same as before introducing the simplefb resource management helpers.

3. Enabling clks/regulators in single loop vs enable as separate step
- simpledrm uses a single loop to both get + enable clks/regulators
  this means that if 1 clk/regulator returns -EPROBE_DEFER previously
  gotten + enabled clks/regulators will get disabled
- simplefb first gets all clks and regulators and attaches power-domains
  and only after doing that successfully does it enable clks and regulators

The simpledrm behavior here, with it disabling clks/regulators if a later
clk/regulator returns -EPROBE_DEFER is undesirable. The whole purpose of
having the clks/regulators in the simple-framebuffer DT node is keeping
them on.

The new simplefb resource management helpers follow the simplefb model.

4. A behavior change in the new helpers is calling dev_err_probe() before
checking for EPROBE_DEFER, so that the kernel's deferred_probe_timeout
handling will log a defer reason if simpledrm/simplefb fail to bind
indefinitely due to missing clk/regulator/pd drivers.

5. The dev_get_platdata(&pdev->dev) checks from the original code are also
dropped. These checks are not necessary since simple-frambuffer platform-
devices instantiated with platform_data set never have an of_node.

The simplefb and simpledrm drivers will be moved over to these new
helpers in follow-up patches.

Signed-off-by: Hans de Goede <johannes.goede@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
